.TH "libnvmf_config_get_hostid" 9 "libnvmf_config_get_hostid" "October 2026" "libnvme API manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
libnvmf_config_get_hostid \- the top-level [Host] host ID.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "const char *" libnvmf_config_get_hostid
.BI "(const struct libnvmf_config *config "  ");"
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP "config" 12
the resolved configuration
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
See \fBlibnvmf_config_get_hostnqn\fP.
.SH "RETURN"
borrowed string, valid while \fIconfig\fP is alive, or NULL when the
top-level file names no host ID (the caller falls back to the system
identity in /etc/nvme/hostid).
